// ── HEADER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// @version=6
//
// @description   This library implements a comprehensive set of mathematical and
//                statistical functions for quantitative analysis in Pine Script™.
//                It integrates a custom weighting series (e.g., volume, tick count)
//                into standard and advanced statistical calculations, focusing on
//                **Weighted Least Squares (WLS)** and the **Law of Total Moments**.
//
//                This architecture allows for a structural decomposition of statistics,
//                separating market microstructure (Within-Bar) from trend components
//                (Between-Bar) and noise (Residuals).
//
//                1.  Effective Sample Size (Kish's N_eff):
//                    Standard deviation and standard errors are dynamically corrected
//                    for the reduction in information caused by weighting concentration.
//                    Formula: N_eff = (Σw)² / Σ(w²)
//
//                2.  Moment Decomposition (Law of Total Moments):
//                    Decomposes statistics into additive structural components.
//                    This allows analyzing whether volatility or skewness originates
//                    from the trend direction or the intrabar noise.
//                    • Variance: σ²_tot = σ²_btw + E[σ²_wtn]
//                    • Skewness: M3_tot = M3_btw + E[M3_wtn] + Interaction
//
//                3.  Advanced Bias Correction (Rimoldini, 2013):
//                    Implements exact correction factors for weighted Skewness
//                    and Kurtosis to ensure unbiased estimators for population
//                    statistics, even under heavy weighting.
//                    • Skew_unb = g₁ * [ (Σw(Σw²-w)) / ( (Σw)³ - 3ΣwΣw² + 2Σw³ ) ]^(1/2) ...
//
//                4.  Relationship Analysis (Covariance & Correlation):
//                    A complete suite for analyzing the relationship between two assets,
//                    decomposed into three distinct layers:
//                    • Total:    Correlation of the full price distributions.
//                    • Between:  Correlation of the trend components (Path correlation).
//                    • Residual: Correlation of the noise/residuals (Cointegration proxy).
//                    All correlation functions (`w...Cor`) are normalized using
//                    mathematically consistent weighted standard deviations.
//
//                5.  Weighted Least Squares (Linear Regression):
//                    Performs regression analysis where bars are weighted by importance.
//                    Decomposes the Total Variance into:
//                    • Explained Variance (Trend)
//                    • Residual Variance (Noise around trend)
//                    • Within Variance (Microstructure)
//                    Key Metrics: `wSlopeStdErr` (Reliability), `wResCoVar` (Cointegration).
//
//                6.  Higher Statistical Moments:
//                    Computes higher-order weighted moments for all decomposition layers:
//                    - Variance (M2): Dispersion measurement.
//                    - Skewness (M3): Asymmetry of the distribution (Tail risk).
//                    - Kurtosis (M4): Tail heaviness and outlier frequency.
//
//                7.  Universal Weighting & Fallback Logic:
//                    All functions accept a `weight` parameter. If Σw = 0 (e.g., no volume),
//                    calculations automatically fall back to standard unweighted
//                    equivalents (Uniform Distribution) to ensure stability.
//
//                8.  Standard Weighted Indicators:
//                    Weighted versions of classic technical indicators:
//                    - `wSma`, `wEma`, `wRma` (Wilder), `wHma` (Hull), `wRsi`.
//
//                ---
//
//                **DISCLAIMER**
//
//                This library is provided "AS IS" and for informational and
//                educational purposes only. It does not constitute financial,
//                investment, or trading advice.
//
//                The author assumes no liability for any errors, inaccuracies,
//                or omissions in the code. Using this library to build
//                trading indicators or strategies is entirely at your own risk.
//
//                As a developer using this library, you are solely responsible
//                for the rigorous testing, validation, and performance of any
//                scripts you create based on these functions. The author shall
//                not be held liable for any financial losses incurred directly
//                or indirectly from the use of this library or any scripts
//                derived from it.
library(
  title   = "LibWght")

// ── LOG ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 2026-01-25 0.2.0
// (Ref) Architecture: Complete internal refactoring to modular kernel functions
//       (_calcMom, _calcLRMom, _calcGeom) to ensure mathematical consistency
//       and reduce code duplication.
// (Ref) Internal: Renamed helper '_wgtClean' to '_sanitize' and added '_calcRho'
//       to centralize correlation normalization logic.
// (Mod) API: Removed redundant `midLine` parameter from Residual functions.
//       Geometry is now calculated internally via slope and intercept.
// (Mod) API: Removed default value for `biased` input parameter to enforce
//       explicit decision between Population and Sample statistics.
// (Mod) Returns: Standardized return values of variance functions to
//       `[variance, neff]` (Kish's Effective Sample Size).
// (Add) Higher Moments: Implementation of a comprehensive suite for weighted
//       Skewness and Kurtosis (Between, Residual, Total). Includes exact
//       bias corrections per Rimoldini (2013).
// (Add) Covariance: Added functions for covariance decomposition (`wBtwCoVar`,
//       `wTotCoVar`, `wResCoVar`, etc.) to analyze correlations structure.
// (Add) Correlation: Added full suite of correlation coefficients (`wBtwCor`,
//       `wTotCor`, `wResCor`, `wLRTotCor`, `wLRLocTotCor`) matching the
//       covariance logic.
// (Add) Statistics: New indicator `wSlopeStdErr` to measure the reliability
//       of the regression slope.
// (Mod) API: Standard Deviation (`w...StdDev`) and Standard Error (`w...StdErr`) 
//       functions now return full component decomposition (e.g., [stdTot, stdTrd, stdRes])
//       to allow analysis of volatility sources in price units.
// (Dep) Removed functions wAtr, wTr, and wR.
// (Fix) Math: Critical fix in `wLinReg`. Corrected the determinant calculation
//       fallback logic when the sum of weights is zero (e.g., symbols without volume).
// (Fix) Math: Corrected logic for Skewness bias correction (Sample vs Population)
//       to strictly apply Rimoldini factors only when `biased=false`.
// (Fix) Stability: Introduced Epsilon checks and extended `na` handling to
//       prevent division-by-zero during singularities.
//
// 2025-11-01 0.1.0
// (New) Initial release of library

// ── CONTROL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const string NAME    = "LibWght"
const string VERSION = "0.2.0"
const string STATUS  = "rel"        // "rel", "dev", "dep"

if barstate.isfirst
    switch STATUS
        "rel" => log.info("Library '" + NAME + " " + VERSION + "' released")
        "dev" => log.warning("Library '" + NAME + " " + VERSION + "' in development")
        "dep" => log.error("Library '" + NAME + " " + VERSION + "' deprecated!")
        => runtime.error("Undefined status of library " + NAME + " " + VERSION)

// ── CONSTANTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const float EPSILON = 1e-9

// ── PRIVATE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// @function Sanitises a data series by replacing *na* with 0 and clamping
//           negative values to 0. Use strictly for data that must be
//           non-negative (e.g., Weights, Sigma, Price).
// @param   src   series float  Raw series that may contain *na* or negatives.
// @returns       series float  Clean, non-negative series without gaps.
_sanitize(
  series float src
  ) =>
    series float filled = nz(source = src, replacement = 0)
    math.max(filled, 0)

// @function The core routine for weighted mean.
//           This is the fundamental mean calculation used by all weighted statistics functions.
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param     len      series int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Linear-kernel weighted mean; falls back to
//                                   the arithmetic mean if Σweight = 0.
_calcMean(
  series float source,
  series float wgt,
  series int len
  ) =>
    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    if sumW > 0
        series float sumWS = math.sum(source = wgt * source , length = len)
        sumWS / sumW 
    else
        series float sumS = math.sum(source = source, length = len)
        sumS / len

// @function Calculates the weighted mean (1st moment) and the required central biased moments 
//           (M2, M3, M4) using a numerically stable Two-Pass algorithm.
//           Pass 1: Calculate Weighted Mean.
//           Pass 2: Accumulate central moments using deviations (x - mean).
//           This avoids catastrophic cancellation present in Naïve algorithms (E[x^2] - E[x]^2)
//           when dealing with high-value assets (e.g. Price > 10,000).
// @param    source   series float  Data series (Y).
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series (w).
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length (L).
// @param    needM1   series bool   True if the 1nd moment (mean component) is required.
// @param    needM2   series bool   True if the 2nd moment (Variance component) is required.
// @param    needM3   series bool   True if the 3rd central moment (Skewness component) is required.
// @param    needM4   series bool   True if the 4th central moment (Kurtosis component) is required.
// @returns  [mean, mom2, mom3, mom4]
//           mom1 series float  The weighted mean (E[X]).
//           mom2 series float  The biased 2nd central moment (M₂), NA if not requested.
//           mom3 series float  The biased 3rd central moment (M₃), NA if not requested.
//           mom4 series float  The biased 4th central moment (M₄), NA if not requested.
_calcMom(
  series float source,
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series bool needM1,
  series bool needM2,
  series bool needM3,
  series bool needM4
  ) =>
    series bool calcM4 = needM4
    series bool calcM3 = needM3 or calcM4
    series bool calcM2 = needM2 or calcM3
    series bool calcM1 = needM1 or calcM2
    
    series float mom1 = na
    series float mom2 = na
    series float mom3 = na
    series float mom4 = na

    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    series bool  useW = sumW > 0
    
    if calcM1
        series float mean = _calcMean(source, wgt, len)
        mom1 := mean

        if calcM2
            series float cumWDev2 = 0.0
            series float cumWDev3 = 0.0
            series float cumWDev4 = 0.0

            for i = 0 to len - 1
                series float val = source[i]
                series float w   = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
                series float dev = val - mean
                series float dev2 = dev * dev
                
                cumWDev2 += w * dev2
                
                if calcM3
                    cumWDev3 += w * dev2 * dev
                
                if calcM4
                    cumWDev4 += w * dev2 * dev2
            
            series float denom = useW ? sumW : float(len)
            mom2 := cumWDev2 / denom
            mom3 := calcM3 ? cumWDev3 / denom : na
            mom4 := calcM4 ? cumWDev4 / denom : na

    [mom1, mom2, mom3, mom4]

// @function Calculates Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
//           Used to quantify the information content of weighted data.
//           Formula: N_eff = (Σw)² / Σ(w²)
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length.
// @returns           series float  N_eff.
_calcNeff(
  series float wgt,
  series int len
  ) =>
    series float sumW  = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    series float sumW2 = math.sum(source = wgt * wgt, length = len)

    sumW2 > EPSILON ? (sumW * sumW) / sumW2 : float(len)

// @function Calculates the bias correction factor for Variance/Covariance using N_eff.
//           Refactored to use _calcNeff for better modularity.
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length.
// @param    biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @param    df       simple int    Lost degrees of freedom (1 for Mean, 2 for Regression).
// @returns  [crct, neff]
//           crct series float  The correction factor (biased * crct = unbiased).
//           neff series float  Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
_calcVarCrct(
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series bool biased,
  simple int df
  ) =>
    series float neff = _calcNeff(wgt, len)
    series float crct = 1.0

    if not biased
        series float denom = neff - float(df)
        if denom > EPSILON
            crct := neff / denom
        else
            crct := na
    
    [crct, neff]

// @function Calculates the bias correction factor for Skewness (Rimoldini/Fisher).
//           Used to convert biased population skewness to unbiased sample skewness.
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Look-back length.
// @param    biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns           series float  The correction factor (multiply biased skewness by this).
_calcSkwCrct(
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series float crct = 1.0
    
    if not biased
        series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
        if sumW > 0
            // Rimoldini Exact Factor
            series float sumW2  = math.sum(source = wgt * wgt, length = len)
            series float sumW3  = math.sum(source = wgt * wgt * wgt, length = len)
            series float sumWP2 = sumW * sumW
            series float sumWP3 = sumWP2 * sumW

            series float denom  = sumWP3 - 3 * sumW * sumW2 + 2 * sumW3
            series float termB  = sumWP2 - sumW2
            
            if denom > EPSILON and termB > 0
                crct := (termB * math.sqrt(termB)) / denom
            else
                crct := na
        else
            // Fisher-Pearson Factor
            if len > 2
                series float neff = float(len)
                crct := math.sqrt(neff * (neff - 1)) / (neff - 2)
            else
                crct := na
    
    crct

// @function Calculates Unbiased Excess Kurtosis from biased moments.
//           Unlike Variance/Skewness, this is not a simple factor multiplication.
//           It reconstructs the value using Rimoldini (weighted) or Fisher (uniform) logic.
// @param    mom2     series float  Biased 2nd central moment (Variance).
// @param    mom4     series float  Biased 4th central moment.
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Look-back length.
// @param    biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns           series float  The unbiased excess kurtosis.
_calcKrtCrct(
  series float mom2,
  series float mom4,
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series float krt = mom2 > EPSILON ? (mom4 / (mom2 * mom2)) - 3.0 : na
    
    if not biased
        series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
        if sumW > 0
            // Rimoldini Logic using Weight Sums
            series float wgt2 = wgt * wgt
            series float wgt3 = wgt2 * wgt
            series float wgt4 = wgt3 * wgt

            series float sumW2 = math.sum(source = wgt2, length = len)
            series float sumW3 = math.sum(source = wgt3, length = len)
            series float sumW4 = math.sum(source = wgt4, length = len)

            series float sumWP2  = sumW * sumW
            series float sumWP4  = sumWP2 * sumWP2
            series float sumW2P2 = sumW2 * sumW2

            series float termA = sumWP2 * (sumWP4 - 4 * sumW * sumW3 + 3 * sumW2P2)
            series float termB = sumWP2 * (sumWP4 - 2 * sumWP2 * sumW2 + 4 * sumW * sumW3 - 3 * sumW2P2)
            
            series float termDA = sumWP2 - sumW2
            series float termDB = sumWP4 - 6 * sumWP2 * sumW2 + 8 * sumW * sumW3 + 3 * sumW2P2 - 6 * sumW4
            series float termD  = termDA * termDB

            series float denom = termD * mom2 * mom2
            if denom > EPSILON
                krt := (termA * mom4 - 3 * termB * mom2 * mom2) / denom
            else
                krt := na
        else
            if len > 3
                // Fisher-Pearson Fallback
                series float neff  = float(len)
                series float g2    = krt
                series float num   = neff - 1
                series float denom = (neff - 2) * (neff - 3)
                    
                krt := (num / denom) * ((neff + 1) * g2 + 6)
            else
                krt := na
    
    krt

// @function Calculates the weighted covariance and variances of two series using a
//           numerically stable **Two-Pass algorithm** (Centered Moments).
//           Pass 1: Calculates the weighted means of X and Y.
//           Pass 2: Accumulates the product of deviations: Σw * (x - x̄) * (y - ȳ).
//
//           This approach is strictly preferred over the naive computational formula
//           (E[XY] - E[X]E[Y]) for financial time series, as it prevents
//           "catastrophic cancellation" when price levels are high relative to
//           their volatility (e.g., BTC, JPY, Indices).
// @param    sourceX  series float  First data series (X).
// @param    sourceY  series float  Second data series (Y).
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Look-back length.
// @returns  [cov, varX, varY, meanX, meanY]
//           cov      series float  The weighted biased covariance (Cov[X,Y]).
//           varX     series float  The weighted biased variance of X (σ²x).
//           varY     series float  The weighted biased variance of Y (σ²y).
//           meanX    series float  The weighted mean of X (x̄).
//           meanY    series float  The weighted mean of Y (ȳ).
_calcCoVar(
  series float sourceX,
  series float sourceY,
  series float wgt,
  series int len
  ) =>
    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    series bool  useW = sumW > 0
    series float invW = useW ? 1.0 / sumW : 1.0 / float(len)

    series float meanX = _calcMean(sourceX, wgt, len)
    series float meanY = _calcMean(sourceY, wgt, len)

    series float cumCov  = 0.0
    series float cumVarX = 0.0
    series float cumVarY = 0.0
    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w  = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float valX = sourceX[i]
        series float valY = sourceY[i]
        
        series float dx = valX - meanX
        series float dy = valY - meanY
        
        cumCov  += w * dx * dy
        cumVarX += w * dx * dx
        cumVarY += w * dy * dy
    
    series float cov  = cumCov  * invW
    series float varX = cumVarX * invW
    series float varY = cumVarY * invW

    [cov, varX, varY, meanX, meanY]

// @function Calculates the weighted mean of the residuals around the trend line.
//           This value is theoretically zero in exact WLS, but its calculation 
//           is needed to accurately define the center of the residual distribution
//           when computing higher moments (Skewness and Kurtosis).
//           M(r) ≈ E[Source - Slope * X].
// @param    source   series float  The data series (Y).
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length.
// @param    sumW     series float  The sum of weights (Σw).
// @param    slope    series float  The slope (b₁).
// @returns           series float  The weighted mean residual value (Mean Residual).
_calcResMean(
  series float source,
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series float sumW,
  series float slope
  ) =>
    series bool  useW = sumW > 0

    series float cumWVal = 0.0
    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x = float(len - 1 - i)

        cumWVal += w * (source[i] - slope * x)

    series float denom = useW ? sumW : float(len)
    cumWVal / denom

// @function Calculates the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, and 4th central moments of the residuals (r = source - trend).
//           This highly optimized routine first calculates the mean residual (r̄) using `_calcResMean` 
//           and then performs the accumulation of all required central moments (M₂, M₃, M₄) 
//           in a single, efficient loop.
// @param    source   series float  Data series (Y).
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length.
// @param    slope    series float  The slope (b₁).
// @param    sumW     series float  The sum of weights (Σw).
// @param    needM3   series bool   True if the 3rd moment (Skewness component) is required.
// @param    needM4   series bool   True if the 4th moment (Kurtosis component) is required.
// @returns  [mom1, mom2, mom3, mom4]
//           mom1 series float  The weighted **Mean Residual** (r̄).
//           mom2 series float  The biased 2nd central moment (Residual Variance M₂).
//           mom3 series float  The biased 3rd central moment (Residual Skewness M₃), NA if not requested.
//           mom4 series float  The biased 4th central moment (Residual Kurtosis M₄), NA if not requested.
_calcResMom(
  series float source,
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series float slope,
  series float sumW,
  series bool needM3,
  series bool needM4
  ) =>
    series bool useW = sumW > 0

    series float meanRes = _calcResMean(source, wgt, len, sumW, slope)
    
    series float cumWRes2  = 0.0
    series float cumWRes3  = 0.0
    series float cumWRes4  = 0.0
    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x = float(len - 1 - i)
        
        series float res  = source[i] - (slope * x) - meanRes
        series float res2 = res * res
        
        cumWRes2 += w * res2
        
        if needM3
            cumWRes3 += w * res2 * res
            
        if needM4
            cumWRes4 += w * res2 * res2

    series float denom = useW ? sumW : float(len)
    
    series float mom1 = meanRes
    series float mom2 = cumWRes2 / denom
    series float mom3 = needM3 ? cumWRes3 / denom : na
    series float mom4 = needM4 ? cumWRes4 / denom : na
    
    [mom1, mom2, mom3, mom4]

// @function Calculates the weighted moments of the time axis (X-axis) for use in 
//           Weighted Least Squares (WLS) regression components.
//           Uses Two-Pass algorithm for stability in Variance of X.
// @param    wgt      series float  Clean weight series.
// @param    len      series int    Lookback length.
// @param    sumW     series float  The sum of weights (Σw).
// @returns  [meanX, varX, tssX]
//           meanX series float  The weighted mean of the X-axis (x̄).
//           varX  series float  The weighted variance of the X-axis (σ²ₓ).
//           tssX  series float  The weighted Total Sum of Squares of the X-axis (TSSₓ = Σw(x - x̄)²).
_calcGeom(
  series float wgt,
  series int len,
  series float sumW
  ) =>
    series bool useW = sumW > 0
    series float invW = useW ? 1.0 / sumW : 1.0 / float(len)

    series float cumWX  = 0.0
    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w  = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x  = float(len - 1 - i)
        cumWX  += w * x
    
    series float meanX = cumWX * invW

    series float cumWDev2 = 0.0
    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w  = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x  = float(len - 1 - i)
        series float d  = x - meanX
        cumWDev2 += w * d * d

    series float varX = useW ? (cumWDev2 * invW) : (float(len * len) - 1.0) / 12.0
    series float tssX = useW ? cumWDev2 : float(len) * varX

    [meanX, varX, tssX]

// @function Core Loop for Linear Regression Moments.
//           Calculates weighted central biased moments for decomposed components
//           relative to a Linear Regression Trend Line.
//           Uses a numerically stable Two-Pass algorithm to prevent catastrophic cancellation.
//
//           Decomposition Logic:
//           1. Global (Total): Moments around the global weighted mean (includes Trend).
//           2. Local (Noise): Moments around the regression line (excludes Trend).
//
//           Crucial Note on 4th Moment (Kurtosis):
//           Unlike Variance (M2) or Skewness (M3), the 4th moment is not simply additive
//           due to complex cross-terms: (A + B)^4 != A^4 + B^4.
//           Therefore, 'mom4Tot' and 'mom4Loc' are calculated directly from the
//           deviations to ensure all interaction effects are captured correctly.
//
// @param    mu       series float  Per-bar mean (e.g., HL2).
// @param    sig      series float  Per-bar standard deviation (e.g., (H-L)/2).
// @param    skw      series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness (Input 0.0 if unknown).
// @param    krt      series float  Per-bar intrabar excess kurtosis (Input 0.0 if unknown).
// @param    wgt      series float  Weight series.
// @param    slope    series float  Slope of the regression line (b1).
// @param    len      series int    Look-back length.
// @param    needTrd  simple bool   If true, calculates Total (Global) components including Trend.
//                                  If false, calculates Local components only (Residuals + Within).
// @param    needM3   simple bool   If true, calculates 3rd moments (Skewness).
// @param    needM4   simple bool   If true, calculates 4th moments (Kurtosis).
//
// @returns  [mom2Loc, mom2Tot, mom3Res, mom3Wtn, mom3Trd, mom3Tot, mom3Loc, 
//            mom4Res, mom4Wtn, mom4Trd, mom4Tot, mom4Loc,
//            mom4IntV, mom4IntS, mom4LocIntV, mom4LocIntS]
//
//           -- Variance (M2) --
//           mom2Loc:     Local Variance (Residuals + Within).
//           mom2Tot:     Total Variance (Trend + Residuals + Within).
//
//           -- Skewness (M3) --
//           mom3Res:     Residual Skewness Component.
//           mom3Wtn:     Within-Bar Skewness Component.
//           mom3Trd:     Trend Skewness Component.
//           mom3Tot:     Total Skewness (Sum of components + Interaction).
//           mom3Loc:     Local Skewness (Sum of Res + Wtn + Local Interaction).
//
//           -- Kurtosis (M4) --
//           mom4Res:     Residual Kurtosis Component (Tail risk of noise).
//           mom4Wtn:     Within-Bar Kurtosis Component (Tail risk of microstructure).
//           mom4Trd:     Trend Kurtosis Component (Tail risk of slope changes).
//           mom4Tot:     Total 4th Moment. Calculated DIRECTLY from global deviations
//                        to capture all cross-terms and interactions correctly.
//           mom4Loc:     Local 4th Moment. Calculated DIRECTLY from local deviations
//                        to capture noise interactions correctly.
//           mom4IntV:    Interaction Variance Component (6 * d^2 * sigma^2).
//           mom4IntS:    Interaction Skewness Component (4 * d * Skew * sigma^3).
//           mom4LocIntV: Local version of Interaction Variance (ignoring Trend).
//           mom4LocIntS: Local version of Interaction Skewness (ignoring Trend).
_calcLRMom(
  series float mu,
  series float sig,
  series float skw,
  series float krt,
  series float wgt,
  series float slope,
  series int len,
  simple bool needTrd,
  simple bool needM3, 
  simple bool needM4
  ) =>
    series bool needSkw = needM3 or (needM4 and needTrd)
    series bool needKrt = needM4

    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    series bool  useW = sumW > 0
    series float invW = useW ? 1.0 / sumW : 1.0 / float(len)
    
    series float xBase = float(len - 1)

    series float cumWX = 0.0
    series float cumWM = 0.0

    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x = xBase - i
        series float m = mu[i]
        
        cumWX += w * x
        cumWM += w * m

    series float meanX  = cumWX * invW
    series float meanMu = cumWM * invW

    series float mom2Loc = 0.0
    series float mom2Tot = 0.0 

    series float mom3Res = 0.0
    series float mom3Wtn = 0.0
    series float mom3Trd = 0.0 
    series float mom3Tot = 0.0 
    series float mom3Loc = 0.0

    series float mom4Res = 0.0
    series float mom4Wtn = 0.0
    series float mom4Trd = 0.0 
    series float mom4Tot = 0.0
    series float mom4Loc = 0.0
    
    series float mom4IntV    = 0.0
    series float mom4IntS    = 0.0
    series float mom4LocIntV = 0.0
    series float mom4LocIntS = 0.0

    series bool calcGeom = not needTrd or needM3 or needM4
    series bool calcS3   = needSkw or needKrt

    for i = 0 to len - 1
        series float w = useW ? wgt[i] : 1.0
        series float x = xBase - i
        series float m = mu[i]
        series float s = sig[i]
        
        series float g = needSkw ? skw[i] : 0.0
        series float k = needKrt ? krt[i] : 0.0
        
        series float muDev = m - meanMu
        series float s2    = s * s
        
        series float trdDev  = 0.0
        series float resDev  = 0.0
        series float trdDev2 = 0.0
        series float resDev2 = 0.0
        series float muDev2  = 0.0

        if calcGeom
            trdDev  := slope * (x - meanX)
            resDev  := muDev - trdDev
            trdDev2 := trdDev * trdDev
            resDev2 := resDev * resDev
        
        series float s3 = 0.0
        if calcS3
            s3 := s2 * s

        if needTrd
            muDev2  := muDev * muDev
            mom2Tot += w * (muDev2 + s2)
        else
            mom2Loc += w * (resDev2 + s2)

        if needM3
            series float rawM3Wtn = g * s3
            
            mom3Res += w * (resDev2 * resDev)
            mom3Wtn += w * rawM3Wtn
            
            if needTrd
                mom3Trd += w * (trdDev2 * trdDev)
                series float termInt = 3.0 * muDev * s2
                mom3Tot += w * ((muDev2 * muDev) + rawM3Wtn + termInt)
            else
                series float termIntLoc = 3.0 * resDev * s2
                mom3Loc += w * ((resDev2 * resDev) + rawM3Wtn + termIntLoc)

        if needM4
            series float s4 = s2 * s2
            series float rawM4Wtn = (k + 3.0) * s4
            
            series float resDev4 = resDev2 * resDev2
            mom4Res += w * resDev4
            mom4Wtn += w * rawM4Wtn
            
            if needTrd
                mom4Trd += w * (trdDev2 * trdDev2)
                
                series float termIntVar = 6.0 * muDev2 * s2
                series float termIntSkw = 4.0 * muDev * g * s3
                series float muDev4     = muDev2 * muDev2
                
                mom4IntV += w * termIntVar
                mom4IntS += w * termIntSkw
                mom4Tot  += w * (muDev4 + termIntVar + termIntSkw + rawM4Wtn)
            else
                series float termIntLocVar = 6.0 * resDev2 * s2
                series float termIntLocSkw = 4.0 * resDev * g * s3 
                series float resDev4_Loop  = resDev2 * resDev2
                
                mom4LocIntV += w * termIntLocVar
                mom4LocIntS += w * termIntLocSkw
                mom4Loc     += w * (resDev4_Loop + termIntLocVar + termIntLocSkw + rawM4Wtn)

    series float denom = useW ? sumW : float(len)
    series float invD  = 1.0 / denom

    mom2Loc := not needTrd ? mom2Loc * invD : na
    mom2Tot := needTrd     ? mom2Tot * invD : na

    mom3Res := needM3 ? mom3Res * invD : na
    mom3Wtn := needM3 ? mom3Wtn * invD : na
    mom3Trd := needM3 and needTrd ? mom3Trd * invD : na
    mom3Tot := needM3 and needTrd ? mom3Tot * invD : na
    mom3Loc := needM3 and not needTrd ? mom3Loc * invD : na

    mom4Res := needM4 ? mom4Res * invD : na
    mom4Wtn := needM4 ? mom4Wtn * invD : na
    mom4Trd := needM4 and needTrd ? mom4Trd * invD : na
    
    mom4IntV    := needM4 and needTrd ? mom4IntV * invD : na
    mom4IntS    := needM4 and needTrd ? mom4IntS * invD : na
    mom4LocIntV := needM4 and not needTrd ? mom4LocIntV * invD : na
    mom4LocIntS := needM4 and not needTrd ? mom4LocIntS * invD : na
    
    mom4Tot := needM4 and needTrd ? mom4Tot * invD : na
    mom4Loc := needM4 and not needTrd ? mom4Loc * invD : na

    [mom2Loc, mom2Tot, 
     mom3Res, mom3Wtn, mom3Trd, mom3Tot, mom3Loc, 
     mom4Res, mom4Wtn, mom4Trd, mom4Tot, mom4Loc,
     mom4IntV, mom4IntS, mom4LocIntV, mom4LocIntS]

// @function Helper to calculate correlation coefficient from covariance and std devs.
//           Handles division by zero and clamps result to [-1, 1].
// @param    cov    float Weighted Covariance.
// @param    stdA   float Weighted Standard Deviation of Asset A.
// @param    stdB   float Weighted Standard Deviation of Asset B.
// @returns         float Correlation coefficient.
_calcRho(
  series float cov,
  series float stdA,
  series float stdB) =>
    series float denom = stdA * stdB
    series float rho   = denom > EPSILON ? cov / denom : 0.0
    math.max(math.min(rho, 1.0), -1.0)

// ── PUBLIC ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// @function  Weighted Simple Moving Average (linear kernel).
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Linear-kernel weighted mean; falls back to
//                                   the arithmetic mean if Σweight = 0.
export wSma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 1)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    _calcMean(source, wgt, len)

// @function  Weighted EMA (exponential kernel).
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   simple int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Exponential-kernel weighted mean; falls
//                                   back to classic EMA if Σweight = 0.
export wEma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  simple int length
  ) =>
    simple int len   = math.max(length, 1)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float denW = ta.ema(source = wgt, length = len)
    if denW > 0
        series float numWS = ta.ema(source = wgt * source, length = len)
        numWS / denW
    else
        ta.ema(source = source, length = len)

// @function  Weighted WMA (linear kernel).
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Linear-kernel weighted mean; falls back to
//                                   classic WMA if Σweight = 0.
export wWma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 1)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float denW = ta.wma(source = wgt, length = len)
    if denW > 0
        series float numWS = ta.wma(source = wgt * source, length = len)
        numWS / denW
    else
        ta.wma(source = source, length = len)

// @function  Weighted RMA (Wilder kernel, α = 1/len).
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   simple int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Wilder-kernel weighted mean; falls back to
//                                   classic RMA if Σweight = 0.
export wRma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  simple int length
  ) =>
    simple int len   = math.max(length, 1)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float denW = ta.rma(source = wgt, length = len)
    if denW > 0
        series float numWS = ta.rma(source = wgt * source, length = len)
        numWS / denW
    else
        ta.rma(source = source, length = len)

// @function  Weighted HMA (linear kernel).
// @param     source   series float  Data to average.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Linear-kernel weighted mean; falls back to
//                                   classic HMA if Σweight = 0.
export wHma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series int len = math.max(length, 2)

    series int halfLen = math.max(int(math.floor(len / 2)), 1)
    series int sqrtLen = math.max(int(math.floor(math.sqrt(len))), 1)

    series float fast = wWma(source, weight, halfLen)
    series float slow = wWma(source, weight, len)
    series float diff = 2 * fast - slow

    wWma(source = diff, weight = weight, length = sqrtLen)

// @function  Weighted Relative Strength Index.
//            Applies the weighting kernel to the calculation of Average Gain
//            and Average Loss.
// @param     source   series float  Price series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   simple int    Look-back length ≥ 1.
// @returns            series float  Weighted RSI; uniform if Σw = 0.
export wRsi(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  simple int length
  ) =>
    simple int len   = math.max(length, 1)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float delta = ta.change(source)
    series float gain  = math.max(delta, 0)
    series float loss  = math.max(-delta, 0)

    series float avgGain = wRma(gain, wgt, len)
    series float avgLoss = wRma(loss, wgt, len)

    avgLoss < EPSILON ? 100 : 100 - 100 / (1 + avgGain / avgLoss)

// @function  Weighted Between Variance (biased/unbiased).
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns [variance, neff]
//          variance  series float  The calculated between-bar variance (σ²btw), either biased or unbiased.
//          neff      series float  Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
export wBtwVar(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    [_, varB, _, _] = _calcMom(source, wgt, len, false, true, false, false)
    [crct, neff] = _calcVarCrct(wgt, len, biased, 1)

    [varB * crct, neff]

// @function  Weighted Between Standard Deviation.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  σbtw uniform if Σw = 0.
export wBtwStdDev(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
   ) =>
    [varBtw, _] = wBtwVar(source, weight, length, biased)
    varBtw >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varBtw) : na

// @function  Weighted Between Standard Error.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  √(σ²btw / N_eff) uniform if Σw = 0.
export wBtwStdErr(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [varBtw, neff] = wBtwVar(source, weight, length, biased)
    varBtw >= 0 and neff > EPSILON ? math.sqrt(varBtw / neff) : na

// @function  Weighted Between Skewness (Rimoldini Exact).
//            Uses algebraic expansion for moments and the exact Rimoldini (2013)
//            correction factor for unbiased estimation.
//            Fallback: If total weight is 0, assumes uniform weights and applies
//            standard Fisher-Pearson correction.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  Skewness.
export wBtwSkw(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    [_, mom2, mom3, _] = _calcMom(source, wgt, len, false, true, true, false)
    series float denom = mom2 * math.sqrt(mom2)
    series float skw   = denom > EPSILON ? mom3 / denom : na

    skw * _calcSkwCrct(wgt, len, biased)

// @function  Weighted Between Kurtosis (Rimoldini Exact).
//            Calculates Excess Kurtosis (Normal = 0).
//            Uses algebraic expansion for 4th moment and the exact Rimoldini (2013)
//            correction factor for unbiased estimation with frequency weights.
//            Reference: Rimoldini, R. (2013). "Weighted skewness and kurtosis unbiased by sample size".
//            Fallback: If total weight is 0, applies standard Fisher-Pearson correction for sample size N.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample (Rimoldini corrected).
// @returns            series float  Excess Kurtosis.
export wBtwKrt(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 4)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    [_, mom2, _, mom4] = _calcMom(source, wgt, len, false, true, false, true)

    _calcKrtCrct(mom2, mom4, wgt, len, biased)

// @function  Weighted Between Covariance.
//            Measures how two variables change together using the computational
//            formula: E[XY] - E[X]E[Y].
//            Utilizes joint geometric weights for both the individual means and the
//            joint moment to ensure structural consistency."
// @param     sourceA  series float  First series (X).
// @param     sourceB  series float  Second series (Y).
// @param     weightA  series float  Weight of first series.
// @param     weightB  series float  Weight of second series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  Weighted Covariance.
export wBtwCoVar(
  series float sourceA,
  series float sourceB,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len      = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    [cov, _, _, _, _] = _calcCoVar(sourceA, sourceB, wgtJnt, len)

    [crct, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgtJnt, len, biased, 1) 
    cov * crct

// @function    Weighted Between Correlation.
//              Standard correlation of price paths (Trend Correlation).
// @param       sourceA  series float  Asset A.
// @param       sourceB  series float  Asset B.
// @param       weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param       weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns              series float  Correlation [-1, 1].
export wBtwCor(
  series float sourceA,
  series float sourceB,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)
    series int len      = math.max(length, 2)

    [cov, varA, varB, _, _] = _calcCoVar(sourceA, sourceB, wgtJnt, len)
    
    series float stdA = varA >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varA) : 0.0
    series float stdB = varB >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varB) : 0.0
    
    _calcRho(cov, stdA, stdB)

// @function  Weighted Total Variance (= between-group + within-group).
//            Useful when each bar represents an aggregate with its own
//            mean* and pre-estimated σ (e.g., second-level ranges inside a
//            1-minute bar). Assumes the *weight* series applies to both the
//            group means and their σ estimates.
// @param     mu       series float  Group means (e.g., HL2 of 1-second bars).
// @param     sigma    series float  Pre-estimated σ of each group (same basis).
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series (volume, ticks, …).
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns [varBtw, varWtn, neff]
//          varBtw  series float  The between-bar variance component (σ²btw).
//          varWtn  series float  The within-bar variance component (σ²wtn).
//          neff      series float  Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
export wTotVar(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)

    [crct, neff] = _calcVarCrct(wgt, len, biased, 1)

    [varBtwRaw, _] = wBtwVar(mu, wgt, len, true)
    series float varWtnRaw = _calcMean(sig * sig, wgt, len)

    series float varBtw = varBtwRaw * crct
    series float varWtn = varWtnRaw * crct

    [varBtw, varWtn, neff]

// @function  Weighted Total Standard Deviation Decomposition.
//            Calculates the total standard deviation and its components.
//            Note: Components are NOT additive (σ_tot ≠ σ_btw + σ_wtn), 
//            but related via variance: σ²_tot = σ²_btw + σ²_wtn.
// @param     mu       series float  Group means.
// @param     sigma    series float  Group sigmas.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [stdTot, stdBtw, stdWtn]
//            stdTot   series float  Total Standard Deviation.
//            stdBtw   series float  Between-Bar component (Trend volatility).
//            stdWtn   series float  Within-Bar component (Intrabar volatility).
export wTotStdDev(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
   ) =>
    [varBtw, varWtn, _] = wTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, length, biased)
    
    series float stdTot = math.min(varBtw, varWtn) >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varBtw + varWtn) : na
    series float stdBtw = varBtw >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varBtw) : na
    series float stdWtn = varWtn >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varWtn) : na
    
    [stdTot, stdBtw, stdWtn]

// @function  Weighted Total Standard Error Decomposition.
//            Decomposes the standard error estimate.
//            SE_part = √( Var_part / N_eff ).
// @param     mu       series float  Group means.
// @param     sigma    series float  Group sigmas.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [steTot, steBtw, steWtn]
//            steTot   series float  Total Standard Error.
//            steBtw   series float  Between-Bar Standard Error.
//            steWtn   series float  Within-Bar Standard Error.
export wTotStdErr(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [varBtw, varWtn, neff] = wTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, length, biased)
    
    series float n     = neff > EPSILON ? neff : na
    series float steTot = math.min(varBtw, varWtn) >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt((varBtw + varWtn) / n) : na
    series float steBtw = varBtw >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varBtw / n) : na
    series float steWtn = varWtn >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varWtn / n) : na
    
    [steTot, steBtw, steWtn]

// @function  Weighted Total Skewness (Rimoldini Exact).
//            Combines Between-Bar, Within-Bar, and Interaction moments via
//            algebraic expansion (Law of Total Moments).
//            Formula: M3_tot = M3_btw + M3_wtn + Interaction
//            Interaction = 3 * (E[σ²µ] - E[µ]*E[σ²])
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean (e.g. HL2).
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation (e.g. (H-L)/2).
// @param     skewness series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness (Input 0.0 if unknown).
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [skwBtw, skwWtn, skwInt]
//            skwBtw  series float  Between-Component: Asymmetry of the trend itself (price path).
//            skwWtn  series float  Within-Component: Average asymmetry inside the candles.
//            skwInt  series float  Interaction-Component: Correlation between Price and Volatility.
export wTotSkw(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)

    [meanMu, mom2Btw, mom3Btw, _] = _calcMom(mu, wgt, len, true, true, true, false)

    series float sig2 = sig * sig
    series float sig3 = sig2 * sig

    series float meanSig2   = _calcMean(sig2, wgt, len)
    series float meanSig2Mu = _calcMean(sig2 * mu, wgt, len)
    
    series float mom3Wtn = _calcMean(skw * sig3, wgt, len)
    series float mom3Int = 3 * (meanSig2Mu - meanMu * meanSig2)

    series float varBtw = mom2Btw
    series float varTot = varBtw + meanSig2
    series float denom  = varTot > 0 ? (varTot * math.sqrt(varTot)) : 1.0
    series float crct   = _calcSkwCrct(wgt, len, biased)

    series float skwBtw = denom > EPSILON ? (crct * mom3Btw) / denom : na
    series float skwWtn = denom > EPSILON ? (crct * mom3Wtn) / denom : na
    series float skwInt = denom > EPSILON ? (crct * mom3Int) / denom : na

    [skwBtw, skwWtn, skwInt]

// @function  Weighted Total Kurtosis (Rimoldini Exact).
//            Combines Between-Bar, Within-Bar, and multiple Interaction moments.
//            Calculates Total Excess Kurtosis.
//            Formula Decomposition:
//            M4_tot = M4_btw + E[M4_wtn] + 6*E[d²σ²] + 4*E[d*M3_wtn]
//            where d = (µ - E[µ])
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean.
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param     skewness series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness (0.0 if unknown).
// @param     kurtosis series float  Per-bar intrabar excess kurtosis (0.0 if unknown).
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [krtTot, krtBtw, krtWtn, krtIntVar, krtIntSkw]
//            krtTot    series float  Total Excess Kurtosis (Rimoldini corrected).
//            krtBtw    series float  Between-Bar Component (Scaled additive contribution).
//            krtWtn    series float  Within-Bar Component (Scaled additive contribution).
//            krtIntVar series float  Interaction (Variance) Component (Scaled additive contribution).
//            krtIntSkw series float  Interaction (Skewness) Component (Scaled additive contribution).
export wTotKrt(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float kurtosis,
  series float weight,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 4)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)
    series float krt = nz(kurtosis, 0.0)

    [meanMu, mom2Btw, mom3Btw, mom4Btw] = _calcMom(mu, wgt, len, true, true, true, true)

    series float sig2 = sig * sig
    series float sig4 = sig2 * sig2

    series float rawM3Wtn = skw * (sig2 * sig)
    series float rawM4Wtn = (krt + 3.0) * sig4

    series float meanSig2    = _calcMean(sig2, wgt, len)
    series float meanMuSig2  = _calcMean(mu * sig2, wgt, len)
    series float meanMu2Sig2 = _calcMean(mu * mu * sig2, wgt, len)
    series float meanM3      = _calcMean(rawM3Wtn, wgt, len)
    series float meanMuM3    = _calcMean(mu * rawM3Wtn, wgt, len)
    series float mom4Wtn     = _calcMean(rawM4Wtn, wgt, len)

    series float mom4IntVar = 6.0 * (meanMu2Sig2 - 2 * meanMu * meanMuSig2 + meanMu * meanMu * meanSig2)
    series float mom4IntSkw = 4.0 * (meanMuM3 - meanMu * meanM3)

    series float mom4Tot = mom4Btw + mom4Wtn + mom4IntVar + mom4IntSkw

    series float varBtw = mom2Btw
    series float varTot = varBtw + meanSig2

    series float krtTotU = _calcKrtCrct(varTot, mom4Tot, wgt, len, biased) 
    series float ratio   = math.abs(mom4Tot) > EPSILON ? krtTotU / mom4Tot : 0.0

    series float krtBtw  = ratio * mom4Btw
    series float krtWtn  = ratio * mom4Wtn
    series float krtIntV = ratio * mom4IntVar
    series float krtIntS = ratio * mom4IntSkw

    [krtTotU, krtBtw, krtWtn, krtIntV, krtIntS]

// @function  Weighted Total Covariance Decomposition.
//            Decomposes the total covariance into its "Between" and "Within" components
//            based on the Law of Total Covariance.
//            Allows analyzing whether correlation comes from the trend (Between)
//            or the microstructure/noise (Within).
// @param     muA      series float  Mean of Asset A (e.g. HL2).
// @param     muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param     coVar    series float  Per-bar intrabar covariance (Input).
// @param     weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param     weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [covBtw, covWtn]
//            covBtw   series float  Between-Bar Covariance (Trend correlation).
//            covWtn   series float  Average Within-Bar Covariance (Intrabar correlation).
export wTotCoVar(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len      = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    [crct, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgtJnt, len, biased, 1)

    series float covBtwRaw = wBtwCoVar(muA, muB, wgtA, wgtB, len, true)
    series float covWtnRaw = _calcMean(coVar, wgtJnt, len)

    series float covBtw = covBtwRaw * crct
    series float covWtn = covWtnRaw * crct

    [covBtw, covWtn]

// @function    Weighted Total Correlation Decomposition.
//              Calculates the total correlation and decomposes it into its structural components.
//              All components are normalized by their respective joint-weighted standard deviations.
// @param       muA      series float  Mean of Asset A (e.g. HL2).
// @param       muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param       sigmaA   series float  Sigma of Asset A.
// @param       sigmaB   series float  Sigma of Asset B.
// @param       coVar    series float  Intrabar Covariance.
// @param       weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param       weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns     [corrTot, corrBtw, corrWtn]
//              corrTot  series float  Total Correlation.
//              corrBtw  series float  Between-Bar Correlation (Trend similarity).
//              corrWtn  series float  Within-Bar Correlation (Microstructure similarity).
export wTotCor(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float sigmaA,
  series float sigmaB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    [covBtw, covWtn] = wTotCoVar(muA, muB, coVar, wgtA, wgtB, length, true)
    series float covTot = covBtw + covWtn
    
    [varBtwA, varWtnA, _] = wTotVar(muA, sigmaA, wgtJnt, length, true)
    [varBtwB, varWtnB, _] = wTotVar(muB, sigmaB, wgtJnt, length, true)
    
    series float stdTotA = math.sqrt(varBtwA + varWtnA)
    series float stdTotB = math.sqrt(varBtwB + varWtnB)
    series float corrTot = _calcRho(covTot, stdTotA, stdTotB)

    series float stdBtwA = math.sqrt(varBtwA)
    series float stdBtwB = math.sqrt(varBtwB)
    series float corrBtw = _calcRho(covBtw, stdBtwA, stdBtwB)

    series float stdWtnA = math.sqrt(varWtnA)
    series float stdWtnB = math.sqrt(varWtnB)
    series float corrWtn = _calcRho(covWtn, stdWtnA, stdWtnB)
    
    [corrTot, corrBtw, corrWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear Regression.
// @param     source   series float   Data series.
// @param     weight   series float   Weight series.
// @param     length   series int     Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @returns [estimate, slope, intercept]
//          estimate   series float  The estimated value of the regression line at the most recent bar.
//          slope      series float  The slope of the regression line.
//          intercept  series float  The intercept of the regression line.
export wLinReg(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float x   = float(bar_index)
    
    [covXY, varX, _, meanX, meanY] = _calcCoVar(x, source, wgt, len)

    series float slope     = math.abs(varX) > EPSILON ? covXY / varX : 0.0
    series float intercept = meanY - slope * meanX
    series float estimate  = intercept + slope * x

    [estimate, slope, intercept]

// @function  Weighted Least Square Moving Average.
// @param     source   series float   Data series.
// @param     weight   series float   Weight series.
// @param     length   series int     Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @returns            series float   Least square weighted mean. Falls back
//                                    to unweighted regression if Σw = 0.
export wLSma(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series int length
  ) =>
    [estimate, _, _] = wLinReg(source, weight, length)
    estimate

// @function  Weighted Residual Variance.
//            linear regression – optionally biased (population) or
//            unbiased (sample).
// @param     source     series float   Data series.
// @param     weight     series float   Weighting series (volume, etc.).
// @param     slope      series float   Slope per bar.
// @param     length     series int     Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased     series bool    true  → population variance (σ²_P), denominator ≈ N_eff.
//                                      false → sample variance (σ²_S), denominator ≈ N_eff - 2.
//                                              (Adjusts for 2 degrees of freedom lost to the regression).
// @returns [variance, neff]
//          variance  series float  The calculated residual variance (σ²res), either biased or unbiased.
//          neff      series float  Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
export wResVar(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)

    [_, varResB, _, _] = _calcResMom(source, wgt, len, slope, sumW, false, false)
    [crct, neff] = _calcVarCrct(wgt, len, biased, 2)

    [varResB * crct, neff]

// @function  Weighted Residual Standard Deviation.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope per bar.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  σres; uniform if Σw = 0.
export wResStdDev(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
   ) =>
    [varRes, _] = wResVar(source, weight, slope, length, biased)
    varRes >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varRes) : na

// @function  Weighted Residual Standard Error.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope per bar.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population (biased); false → sample.
// @returns            series float  √(σ²res / N_eff); uniform if Σw = 0.
export wResStdErr(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [varRes, neff] = wResVar(source, weight, slope, length, biased)
    varRes >= 0 and neff > EPSILON ? math.sqrt(varRes / neff) : na

// @function  Weighted Residual Skewness.
//            Measures the asymmetry of the residuals (noise) around the regression line.
//            Uses exact Rimoldini correction.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns            series float  Residual Skewness.
export wResSkw(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float sumW  = math.sum(source = wgt,  length = len)
    
    [_, mom2, mom3, _] = _calcResMom(source, wgt, len, slope, sumW, true, false)
    series float denom = mom2 * math.sqrt(mom2)
    series float skw   = denom > EPSILON ? mom3 / denom : na

    skw *  _calcSkwCrct(wgt, len, biased)

// @function  Weighted Residual Kurtosis.
//            Measures the "fatness" of the tails of the residuals.
//            High Kurtosis: Trend is prone to extreme outlier shocks.
//            Uses exact Rimoldini correction for Excess Kurtosis.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns            series float  Residual Excess Kurtosis.
export wResKrt(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt,  length = len)
    
    [_, mom2, _, mom4] = _calcResMom(source, wgt, len, slope, sumW, false, true)

    _calcKrtCrct(mom2, mom4, wgt, len, biased)

// @function  Weighted Residual Covariance (Optimized).
//            Measures the co-movement of the noise (residuals) of two assets.
//            Uses Covariance Decomposition: Cov(Res) = Cov(Btw) - Cov(Trend).
//            Cov(Trend) = SlopeA * SlopeB * Var(X).
//            This metric is mathematically related to the analysis of cointegration.
// @param     sourceA  series float  Asset A.
// @param     sourceB  series float  Asset B.
// @param     weightA  series float  Weight of A.
// @param     weightB  series float  Weight of B.
// @param     slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param     slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns            series float  Residual Covariance.
export wResCoVar(
  series float sourceA,
  series float sourceB,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len      = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    series float sumWJnt = math.sum(source = wgtJnt, length = len)

    [_, varX, _] = _calcGeom(wgtJnt, len, sumWJnt)
    series float covBtw = wBtwCoVar(sourceA, sourceB, wgtA, wgtB, len, true)
    series float covTrd = slopeA * slopeB * varX
    series float covRes = covBtw - covTrd

    [crct, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgtJnt, len, biased, 2) 
    covRes * crct 

// @function    Weighted Residual Correlation.
//              Correlation of the noise (residuals) after removing the linear trends.
//              High values indicate that assets mean-revert together (Cointegration proxy).
// @param       sourceA  series float  Asset A.
// @param       sourceB  series float  Asset B.
// @param       weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param       weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param       slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param       slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns              series float  Correlation [-1, 1].
export wResCor(
  series float sourceA,
  series float sourceB,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    series float covRes = wResCoVar(sourceA, sourceB, wgtA, wgtB, slopeA, slopeB, length, true)
    
    series float stdA = wResStdDev(sourceA, wgtJnt, slopeA, length, true)
    series float stdB = wResStdDev(sourceB, wgtJnt, slopeB, length, true)
    
    _calcRho(covRes, stdA, stdB)

// @function    Weighted Standard Error of the Slope.
//              Measures the reliability of the estimated trend slope.
//              Formula: Sqrt( UnbiasedResVar / TSS_x )
//              where TSS_x is the Total Sum of Squares of the X-axis.
// @param     source   series float  Data series.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns            series float Standard Error of the slope (in units of source per bar).
export wSlopeStdErr(
  series float source,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)

    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)

    [varResU, _] = wResVar(source, wgt, slope, len, false)
    [_, _, tssX] = _calcGeom(wgt, len, sumW)
    math.abs(varResU) < EPSILON ? 0 : tssX > EPSILON ? math.sqrt(varResU / tssX) : na

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Total Variance **around the
//            window’s weighted mean μ**.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean m_i.
// @param     sigma    series float  Pre-estimated σ_i of each bar.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series w_i (≥ 0).
// @param     slope    series float  Slope b₁ of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length ≥ 2.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
//
// @returns [varTrd, varRes, varWtn, neff]
//          varTrd  series float  The trend variance component (σ²trd), explained by the linear regression.
//          varRes  series float  The residual variance component (σ²res).
//          varWtn  series float  The within-bar variance component (σ²wtn).
//          neff    series float  Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
export wLRTotVar(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)

    series float varWtnRaw = _calcMean(sig * sig, wgt, len)
    [varRes, neff] = wResVar(mu, wgt, slope, length, biased)
    series float sumW = math.sum(source = wgt, length = len)
    [_, varXRaw, _]   = _calcGeom(wgt, len, sumW)
    series float varTrdRaw = slope * slope * varXRaw
   
    [crctGen, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgt, len, biased, 1)
    
    series float varTrd = varTrdRaw * crctGen
    series float varWtn = varWtnRaw * crctGen

    [varTrd, varRes, varWtn, neff]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Total Standard Deviation Decomposition.
//            Decomposes volatility relative to the regression line.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean.
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar sigma.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope b₁.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [stdTot, stdTrd, stdRes, stdWtn]
//            stdTot   series float  Total Standard Deviation.
//            stdTrd   series float  Trend component (Explained volatility).
//            stdRes   series float  Residual component (Unexplained volatility).
//            stdWtn   series float  Within component (Microstructure volatility).
export wLRTotStdDev(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [varTrd, varRes, varWtn, _] = wLRTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, slope, length, biased)
    
    series float stdTot = math.min(varTrd, varRes, varWtn) >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varTrd + varRes + varWtn) : na
    series float stdTrd = varTrd >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varTrd) : na
    series float stdRes = varRes >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varRes) : na
    series float stdWtn = varWtn >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varWtn) : na
    
    [stdTot, stdTrd, stdRes, stdWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Total Standard Error Decomposition.
//            Decomposes the standard error of the estimate components.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean.
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar sigma.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope b₁.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [steTot, steTrd, steRes, steWtn]
export wLRTotStdErr(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [varTrd, varRes, varWtn, neff] = wLRTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, slope, length, biased)
    
    series float n = neff > EPSILON ? neff : na
    series float steTot = math.min(varTrd, varRes, varWtn) >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt((varTrd + varRes + varWtn) / n) : na
    series float steTrd = varTrd >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varTrd / n) : na
    series float steRes = varRes >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varRes / n) : na
    series float steWtn = varWtn >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varWtn / n) : na
    
    [steTot, steTrd, steRes, steWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Total Skewness Decomposition (Optimized).
//            Calculates the total skewness and decomposes it mathematically exactly into its components.
//            The method is based on the additive decomposition of the third moments.
//            Formula: M3_tot = M3_trd + M3_res + M3_wtn + M3_inter
//            All components are corrected with the Rimoldini factor and normalized to the
//            total standard deviation.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean (e.g., HL2).
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param     skewness series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness (Input 0.0 if unknown).
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [skwTrd, skwRes, skwWtn, skwLRInt]
//            skwTrd   series float  Trend Component: Asymmetry resulting from the slope and the weight distribution.
//            skwRes   series float  Residual Component: Asymmetry of the noise around the regression line.
//            skwWtn   series float  Within Component: Average asymmetry inside the bars.
//            skwLRInt series float  Interaction Component: Covers correlations between price/volatility and non-linearities.
export wLRTotSkw(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)

    [_, m2Tot,
     m3Res, m3Wtn, m3Trd, m3Tot, _,
     _, _, _, _, _,
     _, _, _, _] = _calcLRMom(mu, sig, skw, na, wgt, slope, len, true, true, false)

    series float m3Int = m3Tot - (m3Trd + m3Res + m3Wtn)

    series float denom   = m2Tot > 0 ? (m2Tot * math.sqrt(m2Tot)) : 0
    series float crctSkw = _calcSkwCrct(wgt, len, biased)

    series float skwTrd = denom > EPSILON ? (crctSkw * m3Trd) / denom : na
    series float skwRes = denom > EPSILON ? (crctSkw * m3Res) / denom : na
    series float skwWtn = denom > EPSILON ? (crctSkw * m3Wtn) / denom : na
    series float skwInt = denom > EPSILON ? (crctSkw * m3Int) / denom : na

    [skwTrd, skwRes, skwWtn, skwInt]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Total Kurtosis.
//            Calculates Total Excess Kurtosis and decomposes the 4th moment 
//            into its components relative to the linear regression trend line.
//            Mathematical Identity: Tot = Trd + Res + Wtn + IntV + IntS.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean (e.g., HL2).
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param     skewness series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness (Input 0.0 if unknown).
// @param     kurtosis series float  Per-bar intrabar excess kurtosis.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [krtTot, krtTrd, krtRes, krtWtn, krtIntVar, krtIntSkw]
//            krtTot    series float  Total Excess Kurtosis (Rimoldini corrected).
//            krtTrd    series float  Trend Component (Tail risks from slope changes).
//            krtRes    series float  Residual Component (Tail risks from noise).
//            krtWtn    series float  Within Component (Tail risks from microstructure).
//            krtIntVar series float  Interaction (Variance): Heteroskedasticity component (6*σ²*d²).
//                                    High values indicate volatility clusters around trend deviations.
//            krtIntSkw series float  Interaction (Skewness): Asymmetry component (4*Skew*d).
//                                    High values indicate skewed candles occur at trend deviations.
export wLRTotKrt(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float kurtosis,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 4)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)
    series float krt = nz(kurtosis, 0.0)

    [_, m2Tot,
     _, _, _, _, _,
     m4Res, m4Wtn, m4Trd, m4Tot, _,
     m4IntV, m4IntS, _, _] = _calcLRMom(mu, sig, skw, krt, wgt, slope, len, true, true, true)
    
    series float krtTotU = _calcKrtCrct(m2Tot, m4Tot, wgt, len, biased)
    series float ratio   = math.abs(m4Tot) > EPSILON ? krtTotU / m4Tot : 0.0
    
    series float krtTrd  = ratio * m4Trd
    series float krtRes  = ratio * m4Res
    series float krtWtn  = ratio * m4Wtn
    series float krtIntV = ratio * m4IntV
    series float krtIntS = ratio * m4IntS

    [krtTotU, krtTrd, krtRes, krtWtn, krtIntV, krtIntS]

// @function  Weighted Linear Regression Total Covariance Decomposition.
//            Decomposes the relationship between two assets into three distinct components:
//            1. Trend Covariance: Covariance of the regression lines.
//            2. Residual Covariance: Covariance of the deviations from the regression lines.
//            3. Within Covariance: Average covariance inside the bars (microstructure).
// @param     muA      series float  Mean of Asset A.
// @param     muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param     coVar    series float  Per-bar exact intrabar covariance.
// @param     weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param     weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param     slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param     slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns [covTrd, covRes, covWtn]
//          covTrd   series float  Trend Covariance.
//          covRes   series float  Residual Covariance.
//          covWtn   series float  Average Within-Bar Covariance.
export wLRTotCoVar(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len      = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)
    
    series float sumWJnt = math.sum(source = wgtJnt, length = len)
    [_, varX, _] = _calcGeom(wgtJnt, len, sumWJnt)

    series float covBtwB = wBtwCoVar(muA, muB, wgtA, wgtB, len, true)
    series float covWtnB = _calcMean(coVar, wgtJnt, len)
    series float covTrdB = slopeA * slopeB * varX
    series float covResB = covBtwB - covTrdB

    [crctRes, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgtJnt, len, biased, 2)
    [crctGen, _] = _calcVarCrct(wgtJnt, len, biased, 1)

    series float covTrd = covTrdB * crctGen
    series float covRes = covResB * crctRes
    series float covWtn = covWtnB * crctGen

    [covTrd, covRes, covWtn]

// @function    Weighted Linear-Regression Total Correlation Decomposition.
//              Decomposes correlation into Trend (Regression), Residuals (Noise), and Within components.
// @param       muA      series float  Mean of Asset A.
// @param       muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param       sigmaA   series float  Sigma of Asset A.
// @param       sigmaB   series float  Sigma of Asset B.
// @param       coVar    series float  Intrabar Covariance.
// @param       weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param       weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param       slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param       slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns     [corrTot, corrTrd, corrRes, corrWtn]
//              corrTot  series float  Total Correlation.
//              corrTrd  series float  Trend Correlation (Slope alignment).
//              corrRes  series float  Residual Correlation (Cointegration).
//              corrWtn  series float  Within Correlation (Microstructure).
export wLRTotCor(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float sigmaA,
  series float sigmaB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    [covTrd, covRes, covWtn] = wLRTotCoVar(muA, muB, coVar, wgtA, wgtB, slopeA, slopeB, length, true)
    series float covTot = covTrd + covRes + covWtn
    
    [varTrdA, varResA, varWtnA, _] = wLRTotVar(muA, sigmaA, wgtJnt, slopeA, length, true)
    [varTrdB, varResB, varWtnB, _] = wLRTotVar(muB, sigmaB, wgtJnt, slopeB, length, true)
    
    series float stdTotA = math.sqrt(varResA + varWtnA + varTrdA)
    series float stdTotB = math.sqrt(varResB + varWtnB + varTrdB)
    series float corrTot = _calcRho(covTot, stdTotA, stdTotB)

    series float stdTrdA = math.sqrt(varTrdA)
    series float stdTrdB = math.sqrt(varTrdB)
    series float corrTrd = _calcRho(covTrd, stdTrdA, stdTrdB)

    series float stdResA = math.sqrt(varResA)
    series float stdResB = math.sqrt(varResB)
    series float corrRes = _calcRho(covRes, stdResA, stdResB)

    series float stdWtnA = math.sqrt(varWtnA)
    series float stdWtnB = math.sqrt(varWtnB)
    series float corrWtn = _calcRho(covWtn, stdWtnA, stdWtnB)
    
    [corrTot, corrTrd, corrRes, corrWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Local Total Standard Deviation.
//            Measures the total "noise" (within-bar + residual) around the trend.
// @returns   [stdLoc, stdRes, stdWtn]
//            stdLoc   series float  Local Noise StdDev (Total Noise).
//            stdRes   series float  Residual StdDev.
//            stdWtn   series float  Within StdDev.
export wLRLocTotStdDev(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [_, varRes, varWtn, _] = wLRTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, slope, length, biased)
    
    series float stdLoc = math.min(varRes, varWtn) >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varRes + varWtn) : na
    series float stdRes = varRes >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varRes) : na
    series float stdWtn = varWtn >= 0 ? math.sqrt(varWtn) : na
    
    [stdLoc, stdRes, stdWtn]

// @function    Weighted Linear-Regression Local Total Standard Error Decomposition.
//              Calculates the Standard Error of the "Local" variance components.
//              "Local" refers to the sum of Residual Variance (Inter-bar noise around the trend)
//              and Within Variance (Intra-bar microstructure).
//              This metric quantifies the sampling variability (uncertainty) of the noise
//              estimation itself, using Kish's Effective Sample Size (N_eff).
//              Formula: SE_part = Sqrt( Var_part / N_eff ).
// @param       mu       series float  Per-bar mean (e.g., HL2).
// @param       sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param       weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param       slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param       biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns     [steLoc, steRes, steWtn]
//              steLoc   series float  Local Standard Error: Uncertainty of the total noise estimate (Res + Wtn).
//              steRes   series float  Residual Standard Error: Uncertainty of the residual variance estimate.
//              steWtn   series float  Within Standard Error: Uncertainty of the within-bar variance estimate.
export wLRLocTotStdErr(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [_, varRes, varWtn, neff] = wLRTotVar(mu, sigma, weight, slope, length, biased)
    
    series float n = neff > EPSILON ? neff : na
    series float steLoc = math.min(varRes, varWtn) >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt((varRes + varWtn) / n) : na
    series float steRes = varRes >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varRes / n) : na
    series float steWtn = varWtn >= 0 and not na(n) ? math.sqrt(varWtn / n) : na
    
    [steLoc, steRes, steWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Local Total Skewness.
//            Measures the total asymmetry of the market noise and microstructure 
//            (Residual + Within components) around the linear trend line.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean.
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param     skewness  series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [skwRes, skwWtn]
//            skwRes   series float  Residual Component: Asymmetry of the noise around the regression line.
//            skwWtn   series float  Within Component: Average asymmetry inside the bars.       
export wLRLocTotSkw(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 2)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)

    [m2Loc, _,
     m3Res, m3Wtn, _, _, m3Loc,
     _, _, _, _, _,
     _, _, _, _] = _calcLRMom(mu, sig, skw, na, wgt, slope, len, false, true, false)
    
    series float crctSkw = _calcSkwCrct(wgt, len, biased)
    series float denom   = m2Loc > 0 ? (m2Loc * math.sqrt(m2Loc)) : na
    
    series float skwLoc = denom > EPSILON ? (m3Loc * crctSkw) / denom : na
    series float skwRes = denom > EPSILON ? (m3Res * crctSkw) / denom : na
    series float skwWtn = denom > EPSILON ? (m3Wtn * crctSkw) / denom : na
    
    [skwLoc, skwRes, skwWtn]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Local Total Kurtosis.
//            Measures the total Excess Kurtosis of market noise and microstructure
//            (Residual + Within components) around the linear trend line.
//            Ignores the trend component.
//            Mathematical Identity: Loc = Res + Wtn + IntV + IntS.
// @param     mu       series float  Per-bar mean.
// @param     sigma    series float  Per-bar standard deviation.
// @param     skewness series float  Per-bar intrabar skewness.
// @param     kurtosis series float  Per-bar intrabar excess kurtosis.
// @param     weight   series float  Weight series.
// @param     slope    series float  Slope of the regression line.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [krtLoc, krtRes, krtWtn, krtIntVar, krtIntSkw]
//            krtLoc    series float  Local Total Excess Kurtosis (Noise tails).
//            krtRes    series float  Residual Component.
//            krtWtn    series float  Within Component.
//            krtIntVar series float  Interaction (Variance): Coupling of Residuals and Microstructure Volatility.
//            krtIntSkw series float  Interaction (Skewness): Coupling of Residuals and Microstructure Skewness.
export wLRLocTotKrt(
  series float mu,
  series float sigma,
  series float skewness,
  series float kurtosis,
  series float weight,
  series float slope,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    series int len   = math.max(length, 4)
    series float wgt = _sanitize(weight)
    series float sig = _sanitize(sigma)
    series float skw = nz(skewness, 0.0)
    series float krt = nz(kurtosis, 0.0)

    [m2Loc, _,
     _, _, _, _, _,
     m4Res, m4Wtn, _, _, m4Loc,
     _, _, m4LocIntV, m4LocIntS] = _calcLRMom(mu, sig, skw, krt, wgt, slope, len, false, true, true)
    
    series float krtLocU = _calcKrtCrct(m2Loc, m4Loc, wgt, len, biased)
    series float ratio   = math.abs(m4Loc) > EPSILON ? krtLocU / m4Loc : 0.0
    
    series float krtRes  = ratio * m4Res
    series float krtWtn  = ratio * m4Wtn
    series float krtIntV = ratio * m4LocIntV
    series float krtIntS = ratio * m4LocIntS

    [krtLocU, krtRes, krtWtn, krtIntV, krtIntS]

// @function  Weighted Linear-Regression Local Total Covariance.
//            Measures the co-movement of the "Total Noise" of two assets.
// @param     muA      series float  Mean of Asset A (e.g. HL2).
// @param     muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param     coVar    series float  Per-bar intrabar covariance (Input).
// @param     weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param     weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param     slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param     slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param     length   series int    Look-back length.
// @param     biased   series bool   true → population; false → sample.
// @returns   [covRes, covWtn]
//            covRes   series float  Residual Covariance. Co-movement of deviations from the regression lines.
//                                   High values indicate Cointegration (mean-reverting together).
//            covWtn   series float  Within Covariance. Average co-movement inside the bars (microstructure).
export wLRLocTotCoVar(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length,
  series bool biased
  ) =>
    [_, covRes, covWtn] = wLRTotCoVar(muA, muB, coVar, weightA, weightB, slopeA, slopeB, length, biased)
    [covRes, covWtn]

// @function    Weighted Linear-Regression Local Noise Correlation Decomposition.
//              Calculates the correlation of the "Local Noise" (Residuals + Within-Bar)
//              and decomposes it into its components.
//              This metric ignores the trend entirely and focuses on the synchronization
//              of market noise and microstructure.
// @param       muA      series float  Mean of Asset A.
// @param       muB      series float  Mean of Asset B.
// @param       sigmaA   series float  Sigma of Asset A.
// @param       sigmaB   series float  Sigma of Asset B.
// @param       coVar    series float  Intrabar Covariance.
// @param       weightA  series float  Weight of Asset A.
// @param       weightB  series float  Weight of Asset B.
// @param       slopeA   series float  Slope of Asset A.
// @param       slopeB   series float  Slope of Asset B.
// @param       length   series int    Look-back length.
// @returns     [corrLoc, corrRes, corrWtn]
//              corrLoc  series float  Local Correlation (Total Noise: Res + Wtn).
//              corrRes  series float  Residual Correlation (Cointegration of daily noise).
//              corrWtn  series float  Within Correlation (Microstructure noise).
export wLRLocTotCor(
  series float muA,
  series float muB,
  series float sigmaA,
  series float sigmaB,
  series float coVar,
  series float weightA,
  series float weightB,
  series float slopeA,
  series float slopeB,
  series int length
  ) =>
    series float wgtA   = _sanitize(weightA)
    series float wgtB   = _sanitize(weightB)
    series float wgtJnt = math.sqrt(wgtA * wgtB)

    [covRes, covWtn] = wLRLocTotCoVar(muA, muB, coVar, wgtA, wgtB, slopeA, slopeB, length, true)
    series float covLoc = covRes + covWtn
    
    [_, varResA, varWtnA, _] = wLRTotVar(muA, sigmaA, wgtJnt, slopeA, length, true)
    [_, varResB, varWtnB, _] = wLRTotVar(muB, sigmaB, wgtJnt, slopeB, length, true)
    
    series float stdLocA = math.sqrt(varResA + varWtnA)
    series float stdLocB = math.sqrt(varResB + varWtnB)
    series float corrLoc = _calcRho(covLoc, stdLocA, stdLocB)

    series float stdResA = math.sqrt(varResA)
    series float stdResB = math.sqrt(varResB)
    series float corrRes = _calcRho(covRes, stdResA, stdResB)

    series float stdWtnA = math.sqrt(varWtnA)
    series float stdWtnB = math.sqrt(varWtnB)
    series float corrWtn = _calcRho(covWtn, stdWtnA, stdWtnB)
    
    [corrLoc, corrRes, corrWtn]